{"name":"Light Lip Gloss","hex":"#e7d9d4","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"light","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Electromagnetic radiation in the wavelength range visible to the human eye (about 400–750 nanometers): visible light.","Electromagnetic radiation in the wavelength range visible to the human eye or in nearby ranges (infrared or ultraviolet radiation)."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To start (a fire).","To set fire to; to set burning."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/light"},{"term":"lip","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-3 language code for Sekpele."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Either of the two fleshy protrusions around the opening of the mouth.","A part of the body that resembles a lip, such as the edge of a wound or the labia."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lip"},{"term":"gloss","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A surface shine or luster.","A superficially or deceptively attractive appearance."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To give a gloss or sheen to.","To make (something) attractive by deception"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/gloss"}],"entries":[{"title":"Lip Gloss","blocks":[{"text":"\"Lip Gloss\" is the debut single by American rapper Lil Mama. It was released June 19, 2007, as the lead single from her debut album, VYP: Voice of the Young People. \"Lip Gloss\" is a percussive hip-hop song."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/4/4d/LilMama_LipGloss.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lip_Gloss","wikidata":"Q3833198"},{"title":"Lip gloss","blocks":[{"text":"Lip gloss is a cosmetic used primarily to give lips a glossy luster, and sometimes to add a subtle color. It is distributed as a fluid or a soft solid The product is available in ranges of opacity from translucent to solid and can have variously frosted, glittery, glossy, and metallic finishes."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ca/Prestige_Cosmetics.jpg/330px-Prestige_Cosmetics.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lip_gloss","wikidata":"Q747675"},{"title":"Lip","blocks":[{"text":"The lips are a horizontal pair of soft appendages attached to the jaws and are the most visible part of the mouth of many animals, including humans. Mammal lips are soft, movable and serve to facilitate the ingestion of food and the articulation of sound and speech. Human lips are also a somatosensory organ, and can be an erogenous zone when used in kissing and other acts of intimacy."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f5/Lips_2023.jpg/330px-Lips_2023.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lip","wikidata":"Q15173"},{"title":"Light","blocks":[{"text":"Light, visible light, or visible radiation is electromagnetic radiation that can be perceived by the human eye. Visible light spans the visible spectrum and is usually defined as having wavelengths in the range of 400–700 nanometers (nm), corresponding to frequencies of 750–420 terahertz. The visible band sits adjacent to the infrared and the ultraviolet, called collectively optical radiation."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fa/Prism_flat_rainbow_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-Prism_flat_rainbow_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Light","wikidata":"Q9128"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7f/Lip_Gloss.JPG/500px-Lip_Gloss.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7f/Lip_Gloss.JPG/500px-Lip_Gloss.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser